The image illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles. The Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image (left) depicts spherical particles with an irregular, "cauliflower-like" surface, highlighting their unique morphology. The dynamic light scattering (DLS) graph (right) shows that Nano-11 has a relatively uniform hydrodynamic diameter, with a peak around 70-80 nm, a size range considered optimal for efficient uptake by dendritic cells as discussed in the associated text.